  "details": "<p>The Amatu are an\u00a0Aramean tribe that is mentioned in two inscriptions of Ninurta-kudurr\u012b-u\u1e63ur of Suhu and one inscription of the Assyrian king Tiglath-pileser III.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A nomadic Aramean tribe that invaded the kingdom of Suhu in the late 9th/early 8th century B.C. and were living in Babylonia by the time Tiglath-pileser III became king of Assyria in the mid-8th century B.C..",
